  "note": "Recto page in two parts. The top (y 0.134-0.501) finishes Example 1.9: a #dbdcde grey panel [0.1129, 0.1341, 0.6859, 0.5014] cut by A2 into eleven alternating blocks - six `box` prose stretches (n=1,3,5,7,9,11) and five displayed equations (n=2,4,6,8,10) - with the thin plain cyan #00adef bar on the inner (left) edge (decorative_image) and the wide white-on-cyan 'EXAMPLE 1.9' label bar on the outer (right) edge at x 0.696-0.738 (major_heading); panel elements are `full` because the panel spans the whole measure. Below it, section 1.9 is TWO-COLUMN: prose (n=13, n=15) in the left column and Fig. 1.15 with its cyan caption in a right column x 0.579-0.870. The two declared columns overlap in x on purpose: the prose measure is the standard recto 0.097-0.687, but the figure intrudes on its right end, so the prose lines that run beside the figure (y 0.59-0.88) stop short at x 0.565 while the lines above and below it reach 0.687 - which is why block n=13's bbox is the wider measure even though most of its lines are narrower. Section heading '1.9 ELECTRIC FIELD LINES' (n=12) is grey #6d6e71 at 1.45x body. No footer_rule. Folio '23' in a pale cyan box in the outer margin; '2022-23' recorded as running_header."
